{"resource":{"id":"react-beginner-guide","title":"React.js — Beginner Guide","category":"Web Development","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"12 min","pages":21,"lastUpdated":"February 2026","tags":["Web Development","React","Hooks"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1633356122544-f134324a6cee?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"A friendly first walk through React.js — JSX, components, props, state, events, conditional rendering, lists, hooks, routing, forms, and API integration with clear analogies and examples."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"s1","label":"1. Why React?"},{"id":"s2","label":"2. Setup & JSX"},{"id":"s3","label":"3. Components & Props"},{"id":"s4","label":"4. State & Events"},{"id":"s5","label":"5. Conditional Rendering & Lists"},{"id":"s6","label":"6. Hooks Introduction"},{"id":"s7","label":"7. Routing"},{"id":"s8","label":"8. Forms"},{"id":"s9","label":"9. API Integration"},{"id":"s10","label":"10. Best Practices"},{"id":"s11","label":"11. Common Mistakes"},{"id":"s12","label":"12. Tips & Tricks"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQs"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"React.js — Complete Tutorial","tag":"Web Development","time":"44 min"},{"title":"React.js — Step-by-Step Learning Guide","tag":"Web Development","time":"23 min"},{"title":"React.js — Cheat Sheet","tag":"Web Development","time":"5 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Understand what React is and why it dominates modern UI development.</li>\n          <li>Read and write JSX, components, and props confidently.</li>\n          <li>Manage state, handle events, and render lists correctly.</li>\n          <li>Use core hooks — <code>useState</code>, <code>useEffect</code> — and route between pages.</li>\n          <li>Integrate REST APIs and handle forms with validation.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. Why React?</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>React is a declarative JavaScript library for building user interfaces from reusable components. You describe <em>what</em> the UI should look like for any state, and React figures out <em>how</em> to update the DOM efficiently.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-sky-500/40 bg-sky-500/10 text-sky-900 dark:text-sky-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><path d=\"M12 16v-4\"/><path d=\"M12 8h.01\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Analogy</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Think of React components like LEGO bricks — small, self-contained pieces you snap together into anything from a button to a full dashboard.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Setup &amp; JSX</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>npm create vite@latest my-app -- --template react\ncd my-app &amp;&amp; npm install &amp;&amp; npm run dev</code></pre></div>\n        <p>JSX lets you write HTML-like syntax inside JavaScript. Under the hood it compiles to <code>React.createElement</code> calls.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>function Greeting() {\n  const name = &quot;Ada&quot;;\n  return &lt;h1&gt;Hello, {name}!&lt;/h1&gt;;\n}</code></pre></div>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1633356122544-f134324a6cee?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — React renders a component tree into the DOM via a virtual DOM diff.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. Components &amp; Props</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Components are functions that return JSX. Props are inputs, like function arguments.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>function Card({ title, children }) {\n  return (\n    &lt;div class=&quot;card&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;h2&gt;{title}&lt;/h2&gt;\n      {children}\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  );\n}\n&lt;Card title=&quot;Welcome&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Body text&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/Card&gt;</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. State &amp; Events</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>import { useState } from &quot;react&quot;;\nfunction Counter() {\n  const [n, setN] = useState(0);\n  return &lt;button onClick={() =&gt; setN(n + 1)}&gt;Clicked {n}&lt;/button&gt;;\n}</code></pre></div>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-red-500/40 bg-red-500/10 text-red-900 dark:text-red-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><path d=\"m21.73 18-8-14a2 2 0 0 0-3.48 0l-8 14A2 2 0 0 0 4 21h16a2 2 0 0 0 1.73-3Z\"/><path d=\"M12 9v4\"/><path d=\"M12 17h.01\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Never mutate state</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Always create new objects/arrays — use the spread operator to copy then override, not direct assignment like <code>user.age = 30</code>.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Conditional Rendering &amp; Lists</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>{isLoggedIn ? &lt;Dashboard /&gt; : &lt;Login /&gt;}\n{items.map((i) =&gt; &lt;li key={i.id}&gt;{i.name}&lt;/li&gt;)}</code></pre></div>\n        <p>Always provide a stable <code>key</code> when rendering lists — never the array index if items can reorder.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. Hooks Introduction</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p><code>useState</code> stores state, <code>useEffect</code> runs side effects after render, <code>useRef</code> holds mutable values that survive renders.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>useEffect(() =&gt; {\n  document.title = \\`Count: \\${n}\\`;\n}, [n]);</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. Routing</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>TanStack Router or React Router lets you map URLs to components without a page reload.</p>\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>&lt;Routes&gt;\n  &lt;Route path=&quot;/&quot; element={&lt;Home /&gt;} /&gt;\n  &lt;Route path=&quot;/about&quot; element={&lt;About /&gt;} /&gt;\n&lt;/Routes&gt;</code></pre></div>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1555066931-4365d14bab8c?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Client-side routing swaps components under a persistent shell.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. Forms</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>function LoginForm() {\n  const [email, setEmail] = useState(&quot;&quot;);\n  return &lt;input value={email} onChange={(e) =&gt; setEmail(e.target.value)} /&gt;;\n}</code></pre></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. API Integration</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>useEffect(() =&gt; {\n  fetch(&quot;/api/users&quot;).then((r) =&gt; r.json()).then(setUsers);\n}, []);</code></pre></div>\n        <p>Prefer TanStack Query for production — it handles caching, retries, and background refresh.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">10. Best Practices</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Keep components small and focused.</li>\n          <li>Lift state up only when siblings need to share it.</li>\n          <li>Use TypeScript for prop safety.</li>\n          <li>Prefer composition over inheritance.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s11\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">11. Common Mistakes</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <table class=\"w-full border-collapse text-sm\">\n          <thead><tr><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Mistake</th><th class=\"border p-2 text-left\">Fix</th></tr></thead>\n          <tbody>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Mutating state directly</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Return a new object with the setter</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Using array index as key</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Use a stable unique id</td></tr>\n            <tr><td class=\"border p-2\">Missing useEffect deps</td><td class=\"border p-2\">Add every referenced value or move it inside</td></tr>\n          </tbody>\n        </table>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s12\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">12. Tips &amp; Tricks</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Install React DevTools browser extension.</li>\n          <li>Use <code>strict mode</code> during development to catch side effects.</li>\n          <li>Name event handlers with a <code>handle</code> prefix.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>React makes UI a function of state. Master components, props, state, and hooks, and everything else builds on top.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Do I need to know JavaScript first?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Yes — modern JS (ES6+, arrow functions, destructuring, async/await) is a prerequisite.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Class or function components?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Function components with hooks. Classes are legacy.</div></details>\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>React or Next.js?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Learn React first, then add Next.js when you need SSR or file-based routing.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Further Reading &amp; References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Educational content. Verify APIs against the latest React documentation (react.dev).</p>\n      </div></section>"}